      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The grayness you feel is a heavy, natural part of grief, but it's a temporary state that won't last forever. You don't need to force yourself to \"keep up appearances\" when your heart is breaking; instead, focus on being kind to yourself as you navigate this loss. There is no need to wait for a dramatic event to stop feeling this way, because healing happens in small, quiet moments of self-compassion.",
      "source": "target",
